  "notes": "Opened frame 0 of plate_wide_25.mp4 (1440x900) at 1x, 3x, 8x, 11x and 14x with gamma-boosted panels, magenta mask overlay, 100px grid, and cream/dark composites. Initial BiRefNet seed retained BOTH gaming-chair headrest wings: image-right a solid slab x838-899 from y246 down to the shoulder seam near y541, and image-left a wedge x455-562 between the neck and the white shelf from y412 down to the shoulder seam near y534. Traced each boundary from row-wise luminance on this frame only (chair lum 12-22 vs t-shirt 28-51 separated the chair/shoulder seam at x470 y538, x490 y528, x510 y523, x530 y513, x550 y498 on the left and x797 y516 to x902 y541 on the right) and wrote two explicit exclude polygons, both held 3-4px inside the chair so nothing on the person is cut. Verified after the edit: cap crown and brim intact, both ears complete including the right ear tip at x820-848 y275-340, jawline, beard and neck contour unbroken, both raised hands and both shoulders whole, mask still one connected component (467797px, bbox 141,55-1244,899), coverage 0.361. Residual noted and accepted: a ~6x10px chair corner at x900-905 y518-528 where the chair meets the right shoulder, and a rounded dark lobe at x487-505 y245-285 that reads as the cap's rear brim edge above the left ear (kept rather than notch the cap). Judged at the delivered cream and dark composites, not only under magnification. Coordinates measured on this recording's own frame; nothing transferred from another take.",
